<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ramon Berenguer I, Count of Barcelona</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1023–<a href="/years/1076">1076</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Ramon Berenguer the Old</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ramon Berenguer I, called the Old, was count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> from 1035 to 1076. He imposed his authority on a rebellious nobility, collected tribute from the Muslim <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifas</a> and bought rights over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carcassonne">Carcassonne</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/razes">Razès</a>, extending Barcelona's reach north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a>. The first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/usatges-of-barcelona">Usatges of Barcelona</a>, the basis of Catalan law, are traditionally attributed to his reign.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ramon-berenguer-i-count-of-barcelona.jpg" alt="Ramon Berenguer I, Count of Barcelona" width="320" height="440" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:RamonBerenguel1prijimatribut.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
